  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Derivatives model the real world: velocity and acceleration, related rates, and local linear approximation.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Rates in context",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For motion, \\( v(t)=s'(t) \\) and \\( a(t)=v'(t) \\). <strong>Related rates</strong> differentiate a relationship with respect to time. <strong>Linearization</strong>: \\( L(x)=f(a)+f'(a)(x-a) \\). <strong>L'Hôpital's rule</strong> resolves \\( \\tfrac00 \\) and \\( \\tfrac{\\infty}{\\infty} \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Motion",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( v=s',\\ a=v' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Related rates",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "differentiate in \\( t \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Linearization",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(a)+f'(a)(x-a) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "L'Hôpital",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\lim\\dfrac{f}{g}=\\lim\\dfrac{f'}{g'} \\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "wide": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A particle has position \\( s(t)=t^{3}-6t^{2} \\). When is it at rest?</p>\\[ v(t)=3t^{2}-12t=3t(t-4)=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ t=0,\\ 4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Related rates",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A spherical balloon is inflated so its volume increases at 10 cm³/s. How fast is the radius increasing when \\(r=5\\) cm?</p>\\[V=\\tfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\frac{dV}{dt}=4\\pi r^2\\frac{dr}{dt}.\\]\\[10=4\\pi(25)\\frac{dr}{dt}\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\frac{dr}{dt}=\\frac{10}{100\\pi}=\\frac{1}{10\\pi}\\approx0.032\\text{ cm/s}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Use L'Hôpital's rule to evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\dfrac{e^x-1-x}{x^2}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Form \\(0/0\\). Apply once: \\(\\dfrac{e^x-1}{2x}\\). Still \\(0/0\\). Apply again: \\(\\dfrac{e^x}{2}\\to\\dfrac{1}{2}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
